    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n100516" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνηγορ-ία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>advocacy of</i> another's
				<i>cause</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.7
			</span></i> (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ -ίας ἐπιρρωννύντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Ir.</u>
					p.65
				</span></i>
			 W.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὴν -ίαν τοῦ ἴδια πάθη γίνεσθαι
					γυναικῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					2.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.578
			</span></i>; <i>right to practise as an advocate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PGiss.
				40 ii 4
			</span></i><span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τῶν συμμάχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh. Al.</u>
					1425a7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				567.19
			</span></i> (Attalia, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2795
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Aphrodisias</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ συνηγορία τοῦ τι εἶναι</span> the
				<i>affirmative</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				235.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ -ῶν ταμείου</span>”
				<i>sometime advocatus fisci,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					IG
					3.712a
				</span></i>
			.</div>
